  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Metropolitan Security Services recorded $124M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Metropolitan Security Services received 124 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $996K. Metropolitan Security Services' obligations fell 77.0% year over year compared with the prior fiscal period. Metropolitan Security Services' multi-year trend shows obligations that rose from $228M in FY22 to $537M in FY26 before the FY27 drop to $124M. The Department of Justice is the dominant buyer, obligating $123M to Metropolitan Security Services in FY2027 to date. The District of Columbia Courts obligated $675K to Metropolitan Security Services in FY2027 to date. The page note clarifies that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, and that current-year totals are partial. This snapshot captures current-year scale, recent volatility, and the concentration of FY2027 obligations among a small number of buyers.",
